ard internal energy change for the reaction at 298 K?</p></li><li><p>OF₂(g) + H₂O(g) → O₂(g) + 2HF(g);  ΔH° = −310 kJ</p></li></ol><p></p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"chapterId\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:35:29.024+00:00\",\"subjectId\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:35:29.024+00:00\",\"chapter_id\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"difficulty\":\"Hard\",\"subject_id\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"explanation\":[],\"chapter_name\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"optionLayout\":\"grid_2x2\",\"questionCode\":\"CHE-THE-9743\",\"questionType\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"subject_name\":\"Chemistry\",\"correctAnswer\":\"A\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"question_code\":\"CHE-THE-9743\",\"question_type\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"correct_option\":\"a\"},\"questionId\":\"c2d72f88-c8d9-42c5-9dd1-055e783b3aaf\"},{\"id\":\"blk-1788170102677-0-23\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"3b609aa6-6486-41bd-95f8-7dc3192f1154\",\"year\":null,\"marks\":4,\"source\":\"System Admin\",\"chapter\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p><strong>Consider the given diagram for 1 mole of a gas X and answer the following question.</strong></p><p><strong>The process A → B represents</strong></p><img src=\\\"/uploads/1788168097967_tdr8a8.png\\\" width=\\\"50%\\\" data-alignment=\\\"center\\\" style=\\\"width: 50%; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\\\"><p></p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"b9a00cac-5226-4005-93c1-2269be3c4cb0\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>isobaric change</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>isobaric change</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"9636a4ae-769c-4077-8ac3-6f87af569619\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>isothermal change</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>isothermal change</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"}