32 g of oxygen to form 68 g of CO₂.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"2b87d16a-a31b-4e1a-86c8-5ef1e957c40d\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>10 g of carbon is heated in vacuum without any change in mass.</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>10 g of carbon is heated in vacuum without any change in mass.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Which of the following statements best explains the law of conservation of mass?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"c\",\"correctOption\":\"c\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":110,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-78fc5dcc-c0e6-44ad-94dc-c4087c4699fb-0.26890416767594094\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"78fc5dcc-c0e6-44ad-94dc-c4087c4699fb\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>100 g of ethylene polymerises to polythene according to the equation:</p><p>nCH₂ = CH₂ → {CH₂ — CH₂}ₙ</p><p>The mass of polythene produced will be</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"e75b99d9-ccec-4efc-9f83-e71bb2dd97cb\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>100 n g</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100 n g</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"fd95552e-521d-4b7a-a7b7-a78bbb3f2023\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>100/n g</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100/n g</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"ad2a9664-dd1b-4454-886e-7f6ecffb1f06\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>100 n/2 g</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100 n/2 g</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"7a15bfcc-ff06-4591-8b4c-b8cf891e35cc\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>100 g</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100 g</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100 g of ethylene polymerises to polythene according to the equation:</p><p>nCH₂ = CH₂ → {CH₂ — CH₂}ₙ</p><p>The mass of polythene produced will be</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"d\",\"correctOption\":\"d\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":111,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-812461c5-e203-4ce5-957f-86588c1fd0ef-0.46336456359180145\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"812461c5-e203-4ce5-957f-86588c1fd0ef\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>In an experiment, 2.4 g of iron oxide on reduction with hydrogen gave 1.68 g of iron. In another experiment, 2.7 g of iron oxide gave 1.89 g of iron on reduction. Which law is illustrated from the above data?</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"908fc23a-275e-4434-a82f-3dedf148c47f\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>Law of constant proportions</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Law of constant proportions</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"f17c9eb6-b648-4807-bf2c-8020a8cd202a\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>Law of multiple proportions</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Law of multiple proportions</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"6a5f1e63-388e-44c6-8699-87bd2d198603\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>Law of conservation of mass</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Law of conservation of mass</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"b389dda1-8f0b-42bf-b7cb-382c71e70363\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>None of these</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>None of these</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>In an experiment, 2.4 g of iron oxide on reduction with hydrogen gave 1.68 g of iron. In another experiment, 2.7 g of iron oxide gave 1.89 g of iron on reduction. Which law is illustrated from the above data?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sect