 be</strong></p><p>CH₃OH(l) + 3/2O₂(g) → CO₂(g) + 2H₂O(l)</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"b\",\"correctOption\":\"b\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":167,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-c2d72f88-c8d9-42c5-9dd1-055e783b3aaf-0.5008925846175966\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"c2d72f88-c8d9-42c5-9dd1-055e783b3aaf\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<ol start=\\\"24\\\"><li><p>What will be the standard internal energy change for the reaction at 298 K?</p></li><li><p>OF₂(g) + H₂O(g) → O₂(g) + 2HF(g);  ΔH° = −310 kJ</p></li></ol><p></p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"a8ba17d0-d2d2-4ef6-8fc9-5c2f89a3d19c\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−312.47 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−312.47 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"d57fb83c-e5d1-45af-9e85-5dfe304345f1\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−125.03 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−125.03 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"27d71f8e-0517-4f8a-b52d-cafc5d2a1647\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−310 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−310 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"dcb36346-d382-4a49-a6c9-cbcf8bac6ed2\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−156 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−156 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<ol start=\\\"24\\\"><li><p>What will be the standard internal energy change for the reaction at 298 K?</p></li><li><p>OF₂(g) + H₂O(g) → O₂(g) + 2HF(g);  ΔH° = −310 kJ</p></li></ol><p></p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"a\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":168,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-144b076d-e964-4aab-8038-1f4