e atmosphere and the cylinder got empty. If the atmospheric pressure is 1.0 atmosphere, calculate the work done by the gas.</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"chapterId\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:14:34.544+00:00\",\"subjectId\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:14:34.544+00:00\",\"chapter_id\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"subject_id\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"explanation\":[],\"chapter_name\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"optionLayout\":\"grid_2x2\",\"questionCode\":\"CHE-THE-1623\",\"questionType\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"subject_name\":\"Chemistry\",\"correctAnswer\":\"B\",\"correctOption\":\"b\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"question_code\":\"CHE-THE-1623\",\"question_type\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"correct_option\":\"b\"},\"questionId\":\"bc58787f-ded4-4993-bb51-03f93d60a2cc\"},{\"id\":\"blk-1788170105297-0-8\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"e13d4ed2-7405-45bd-ac08-683bd1268abf\",\"year\":null,\"marks\":4,\"source\":\"System Admin\",\"chapter\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>A process is called reversible when</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"5f4ec05e-f606-4562-abee-ff811914fdbe\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>surrounding and system change are same</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>surrounding and system change are same</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"715213b6-64a9-4e90-88b2-1d7ef301b487\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>there is no boundary between system and surrounding</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>there is no boundary between system and surrounding</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"8920f2e6-5be6-4dce-ae25-baed77bbe5c6\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>surrounding is always in equilibrium with system</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>surrounding is always in equilibrium with system</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"04dafd05-b519-4ab7-a884-4caf874cfc27\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>system changes into surroundings spontaneously</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>system changes into surroundings spontaneously</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>A process is called reversible when</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"chapterId\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:16:09.638+00:00\",\"subjectId\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-31T07:16:09.639+00:00\",\"chapter_id\":\"b0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380b17\",\"difficulty\":\"Easy\",\"subject_id\":\"a0eebc99-9c0b-4ef8-bb6d-6bb9bd380a12\",\"explanation\":[],\"chapter_name\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"optionLayout\":\"grid_2x2\",\"questionCode\":\"CHE-THE-2435\",\"questionType\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"subject_name\":\"Chemistry\",\"correctAnswer\":\"C\",\"correctOption\":\"c\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"question_code\":\"CHE-THE-2435\",\"question_type\":\"MCQ_SINGLE\",\"correct_option\":\"c\"},\"questionId\":\"e13d4ed2-7405-45bd-ac08-683bd1268abf\"},{\"id\":\"blk-1788170105297-0-9\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"65b60d89-b988-4cc0-8c41-445e7f7fc5a5\",\"year\":null,\"marks\":4,\"source\":\"System Admin\",\"chapter\":\"Thermodynamics\",\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>For an isothermal reversible expansion process, the value of q can be calculated by the expression</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"d2578de5-4d88-4675-b5ca-2ee2ca8a1765\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>q = 2.303nRT log(V₂/V₁)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>q = 2.303nRT log(V₂/V₁)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"8455aaa5-c0b1-4ebc-8076-5a3738b8da0e\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>q = −2.303nRT log(V₂/V₁)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>q = −2.303nRT log(V₂/V₁)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{