 heated to give steam.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"852f9f5b-facf-41d9-89e1-912f081a6684\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>A sample of N₂ gas is heated at constant pressure without any change in mass.</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>A sample of N₂ gas is heated at constant pressure without any change in mass.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"55a071fd-9073-4617-bc0a-918116a6d9f6\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>36 g of carbon combines with 32 g of oxygen to form 68 g of CO₂.</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>36 g of carbon combines with 32 g of oxygen to form 68 g of CO₂.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"2b87d16a-a31b-4e1a-86c8-5ef1e957c40d\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>10 g of carbon is heated in vacuum without any change in mass.</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>10 g of carbon is heated in vacuum without any change in mass.</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Which of the following statements best explains the law of conservation of mass?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"c\",\"correctOption\":\"c\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":110,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-78fc5dcc-c0e6-44ad-94dc-c4087c4699fb-0.6746803757492678\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"78fc5dcc-c0e6-44ad-94dc-c4087c4699fb\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>100 g of ethylene polymerises to polythene according to the equation:</p><p>nCH₂ = CH₂ → {CH₂ — CH₂}ₙ</p><p>The mass of polythene produced will be</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"e75b99d9-ccec-4efc-9f83-e71bb2dd97cb\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>100 n g</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>100 n g</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"fd95552e-521d-4b7a-a7b7-a78bbb3f20