 volume. It resulted in the increase in temperature of the system from 298 to 323 K. What is the change in internal energy of the system?</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"ae3ca408-6882-4b58-8d85-b2bf406a3b90\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>400 J</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>400 J</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"0d684ca0-de18-4fd4-b1b6-4e2782f330fd\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>200 J</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>200 J</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"3d47b8fa-bf3e-4b2a-ae30-4f20684ce258\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>50 J</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>50 J</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"1f42335b-a632-4351-84f8-fb4b63a64243\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>150 J</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>150 J</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>200 joules of heat was supplied to a system at constant volume. It resulted in the increase in temperature of the system from 298 to 323 K. What is the change in internal energy of the system?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"b\",\"correctOption\":\"b\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":157,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-eb564c39-52b6-4dcf-a988-20b62574fa4a-0.7141782837686618\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"eb564c39-52b6-4dcf-a988-20b62574fa4a\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>One mole of an ideal gas is expanded isothermally and reversibly from an initial pressure of 1.0 bar to a final pressure of 0.1 bar at a constant temperature of 273 K. Which of the following statements is correct regarding this context?</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"b25bde0a-c829-43a8-a17c-671ece51a1e8\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>ΔU = q = 5227 J, W = 0</p>\