<p>&gt; 80.25 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>&gt; 80.25 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"7f269ffc-dc30-4067-af23-4651dd0a4aba\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>&lt; 80.25 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>&lt; 80.25 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"5dde8c8e-7a01-4272-9773-ef11b1e0ce49\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>60.50 kJ</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>60.50 kJ</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>If the heat change at constant volume for decomposition of silver oxide is 80.25 kJ, what will be the heat change at constant pressure?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"b\",\"correctOption\":\"b\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":159,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-4cf4c08a-a3cd-4bc0-8835-4ede50a032ff-0.6983888050111867\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"4cf4c08a-a3cd-4bc0-8835-4ede50a032ff\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>Which of the following relationships is not correct for the relation between ΔH and ΔU?</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"f8d9e2f8-2ca4-4791-b2a1-364e62a4ec7f\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ = 0 then ΔH = ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ = 0 then ΔH = ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"a14fff2a-bda9-4c36-aee9-d89f2ba74750\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ &gt; 0 then ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ &gt; 0 then ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"f4218174-bfcf-4bc9-88cd-acfa8a5cf221\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ &lt; 0 then ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>When Δnᵍ &lt; 0 then ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"a2e15639-2b64-4454-8e17-023aec6bd01d\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>When ΔnᵍRT = 0 then ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>When ΔnᵍRT = 0 then ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>Which of the following relationships is not correct for the relation between ΔH and ΔU?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"d\",\"correctOption\":\"d\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":160,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-387b2401-00a8-448c-9542-83f9aef7e992-0.4442965342703863\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"387b2401-00a8-448c-9542-83f9aef7e992\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p><strong>Consider the following reaction:</strong></p><p>SO₂(g) + ½O₂(g) → SO₃(g)</p><p><strong>How are ΔU and ΔH related for the reaction?</strong></p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"f28fe75c-f9ac-47c9-a65c-e0ff02330486\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − 0.5RT</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − 0.5RT</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"dbf10fb4-faeb-4132-842d-be5a190ffde5\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − RT</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − RT</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"2c9fb185-f216-4ee9-b6e0-918c0656c458\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU + 0.5RT</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU + 0.5RT</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"8d634e9b-8986-4077-b212-1ea5ee9af2d0\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − 1.5RT</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>ΔH = ΔU − 1.5RT</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p><strong>Consider the following reaction:</strong></p><p>SO₂(g) + ½O₂(g) → SO₃(g)</p><p><strong>How are ΔU and ΔH related for the reaction?</strong></p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"a\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":161,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-1b07ee93-dae4-4622-90ad-d167b3a25676-0.8464122142584276\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"1b07ee93-dae4-4622-90ad-d167b3a25676\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>For which of the following reactions will ΔH be equal to ΔU?</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"33ad3577-fd18-4bb5-88eb-29eeb62bc2f0\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>H₂(g) + I₂(g) → 2HI(g)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>H₂(g) + I₂(g) → 2HI(g)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"e154f374-a25c-44a3-a218-11faeda516ea\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>H₂(g) + ½O₂(g) → H₂O(l)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>H₂(g) + ½O₂(g) → H₂O(l)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"dc3607ca-86f0-4b4c-923e-8dcde9cac81b\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>2SO₃(g) → 2SO₂(g) + O₂(g)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>2SO₃(g) → 2SO₂(g) + O₂(g)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"0c634bb0-a6d5-4783-98ba-e57b3ba5c659\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>2NO₂(g) → N₂O₄(g)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>2NO₂(g) → N₂O₄(g)</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>For which of the following reactions will ΔH be equal to ΔU?</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"a\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":162,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-95d6b35c-87f3-436d-86a7-045bfeabb8ac-0.7525569670427089\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"95d6b35c-87f3-436d-86a7-045bfeabb8ac\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p><strong>For combustion of 1 mole of benzene at 25 °C, the heat of reaction at constant pressure is −780.9 kcal. What will be the heat of reaction at constant volume?</strong></p><p>C₆H₆(l) + 7½O₂(g) → 6CO₂(g) + 3H₂O(l)</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"74cffd32-cdad-4299-99f7-78bc89c03c67\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−781.8 kcal</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−781.8 kcal</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"76c63c80-5d96-429e-95a8-4854962bb00b\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>−780.0 kcal</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>−780.0 kcal</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"22607e20-9455-45de-9ca5-d96f4daa35da\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>+781.8 kcal</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>+781.8 kcal</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"4e4367bf-b42d-4667-93f5-0d6cb80425bd\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>+780.0 kcal</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>+780.0 kcal</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p><strong>For combustion of 1 mole of benzene at 25 °C, the heat of reaction at constant pressure is −780.9 kcal. What will be the heat of reaction at constant volume?</strong></p><p>C₆H₆(l) + 7½O₂(g) → 6CO₂(g) + 3H₂O(l)</p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"b\",\"correctOption\":\"b\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":163,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-ff66e9c9-db96-4abc-b095-bd5970e1679f-0.13116583263632275\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"ff66e9c9-db96-4abc-b095-bd5970e1679f\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p>A thermodynamic system consists of a cylinder-piston arrangement with ideal gas in it. It goes from the state i to the state f as shown in the figure. The work done by the gas during the process is</p><img src=\\\"/uploads/1788167993834_6kr5hh.png\\\" width=\\\"50%\\\" data-alignment=\\\"center\\\" style=\\\"width: 50%; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\\\"><p></p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"466e89bc-cd0e-4e19-a135-fbcb5b07cd1f\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>zero</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>zero</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"779231ca-fe91-4313-8d9c-100d9600ff57\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>negative</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>negative</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"c1ffb423-9bb9-4ab3-a669-29171bd2af12\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>positive</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>positive</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"c6dfa66e-728b-4f2f-a571-f431d73febde\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>nothing can be predicted</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>nothing can be predicted</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>A thermodynamic system consists of a cylinder-piston arrangement with ideal gas in it. It goes from the state i to the state f as shown in the figure. The work done by the gas during the process is</p><img src=\\\"/uploads/1788167993834_6kr5hh.png\\\" width=\\\"50%\\\" data-alignment=\\\"center\\\" style=\\\"width: 50%; max-width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto;\\\"><p></p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"a\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":164,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-e21cd7cc-df40-475f-88b2-ee644a4ea28d-0.7186697271024155\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"e21cd7cc-df40-475f-88b2-ee644a4ea28d\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1\",\"text\":\"<p><strong>Two reactions are given below:</strong></p><p>(i) CO<sub>(g)</sub> + ½O₂<sub>(g)</sub> → CO₂<sub>(g)</sub></p><p>(ii) Ag₂O<sub>(s)</sub> → 2Ag<sub>(s)</sub> + ½O₂<sub>(g)</sub></p><p><strong>Which of the following statements is true?</strong></p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"options\":[{\"id\":\"b79b035b-a205-4cce-bfc1-bd3b33ecb65f\",\"key\":\"A\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>For (i) ΔH &lt; ΔU and for (ii) ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>For (i) ΔH &lt; ΔU and for (ii) ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":true,\"option_key\":\"a\"},{\"id\":\"0e0d5748-63fd-4d7a-ae2f-c36f8f5d94f4\",\"key\":\"B\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>For (i) ΔH &gt; ΔU and for (ii) ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>For (i) ΔH &gt; ΔU and for (ii) ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"b\"},{\"id\":\"1a16c8e4-9b00-414c-9118-3f59ea471579\",\"key\":\"C\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>For both (i) and (ii) ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>For both (i) and (ii) ΔH &gt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"c\"},{\"id\":\"fcc937df-6d2a-471d-becd-7d4ad4c51c9f\",\"key\":\"D\",\"content\":[{\"html\":\"<p>For both (i) and (ii) ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"type\":\"text\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p>For both (i) and (ii) ΔH &lt; ΔU</p>\",\"isCorrect\":false,\"option_key\":\"d\"}],\"rawText\":\"<p><strong>Two reactions are given below:</strong></p><p>(i) CO<sub>(g)</sub> + ½O₂<sub>(g)</sub> → CO₂<sub>(g)</sub></p><p>(ii) Ag₂O<sub>(s)</sub> → 2Ag<sub>(s)</sub> + ½O₂<sub>(g)</sub></p><p><strong>Which of the following statements is true?</strong></p>\",\"subject\":\"Chemistry\",\"solution\":[],\"sectionId\":\"sec-2\",\"sectionName\":\"Part B: CHEMISTRY (MCQ)\",\"correctAnswer\":\"a\",\"correctOption\":\"a\",\"negativeMarks\":1,\"questionNumber\":165,\"explanationText\":[]}},{\"id\":\"blk-b8e7a81a-f001-4454-a6b0-0d8db6e20fd8-0.334506117404858\",\"type\":\"question\",\"question\":{\"id\":\"b8e7a81a-f001-4454-a6b0-0d8db6e20fd8\",\"marks\":4,\"content\":[{\"id\":\"blk-1788261338128\",\"text\":\"<p>Which of the following shows <em>dsp²</em> hybridisation and a square planar